Dear FTP Team,

As part of the Bioconductor 3.19 transition, the Debian R team agreed [0] to remove builds for 32-bit architectures (where possible) in line with upstream's cessation of support for 32-bit systems.

Here is the fifth such removal request, this time for r-bioc-rots	. According to dak there should be no issue removing the 32-bit architecture versions of this binary package:

$ ssh mirror.ftp-master.debian.org "dak rm --architecture=armel,armhf,i386 --no-arch-all-rdeps --binary-only --partial --rdep-check --no-action r-bioc-rots"
Will remove the following packages from unstable:

r-bioc-rots |   1.30.0-1 | armel, armhf, i386

Maintainer: Debian R Packages Maintainers <r-pkg-team at alioth-lists.debian.net>

